# Unity tests — Editor open (no CLI batch runs)

Implementation and tests live in **griddungeon-game**. The user typically has that Unity project **open in the Editor**. **Do not** run automated Unity tests from the terminal for now.

## Do not run

- `Unity.exe -batchmode … -runTests` against `griddungeon-game`
- Any shell command that opens the same Unity `projectPath` while the user may be editing

## Do instead

1. **Ask the user** to run **Test Runner → Edit Mode** in the game repo ([Assets/Tests/README.md](https://github.com/miramocha/griddungeon-game/blob/main/Assets/Tests/README.md)).
2. Give **manual Play Mode** steps when closing tickets (see `ticket-test-documentation.mdc`).

## Exceptions

- User explicitly requests CLI tests **and** confirms the Unity project is not open.
- Do not invent test results; rely on user-reported or CI output.
